#META 2026-11-24^November 20, 2026^May 2026 to October 2026 ¶ #NOTE 0~Processing time represents the number of elapsed days between the received date and the first adjudicative decision, which may include RFE response days. We do not include reopened cases. ¶ #NOTE 1~Processing time represents the number of elapsed days between the received date and the first adjudicative decision, which may include RFE response days. We do not include reopened cases. *** If you are a petitioner for an H-2A Temporary Agricultural Worker and your Form I-129 has been pending longer than 15 days and you have not received a decision or a Request for Evidence, you may contact USCIS at (1-800) 375-5283 to inquire about your petition. ¶ #NOTE 2~Since October 2025, H-2A petitioners seeking unnamed beneficiaries can electronically file an H-2A petition with USCIS after the U.S. Department of Labor (DOL) issues a notice of acceptance of the application for temporary labor certification (TLC) and before DOL approves a TLC. However, USCIS will not approve these petitions until after DOL has approved the corresponding TLC. This concurrent processing has contributed to longer H-2A petition processing times because USCIS must now wait until DOL approves the corresponding TLC before we can process the H-2A petition. ¶ #OFF SCD~Service Center Operations (SCOPS) ¶ @I-129^137-E^E - Treaty traders and investors|SCD:21.5:2024-11-06:- ¶ @I-129^137-E3^E3 - Specialty occupation workers from Australia|SCD:5:2026-04-17:0 ¶ @I-129^137-H1B1^H-1B - Specialty occupation - Visa to be issued abroad|SCD:15:2025-07-30:0 ¶ @I-129^137-H1B2^H-1B - Specialty occupation - Change of status in the U.S.|SCD:5:2026-01-02:0 ¶ @I-129^137-H1B3^H-1B - Specialty occupation - Extension of stay in the U.S.|SCD:11.5:2025-10-16:0 ¶ @I-129^137-H2AN^H-2A - Temporary agricultural workers - Named Beneficiary|SCD:15D:2026-07-27:1 ¶ @I-129^137-H2AU^H-2A - Temporary agricultural workers - Unnamed Beneficiary|SCD:15D:2026-07-27:2 ¶ @I-129^13